Third-party software in the tsdb tarball
========================================

tsdb itself is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
only (the file LICENSE in this tarball), except for its client libraries and
the headers they share with the engine, which are under the Apache License 2.0
(LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt; see LICENSING.md and NOTICE). The binaries in this
tarball (bin/, bench/, tests/)
also contain code from the libraries below, which `make dist` links in
statically. Their licenses require that their copyright notice and license
text travel with the binaries; they are reproduced here.

  zstd      BSD License. Zstandard is also offered under GPL-2.0; tsdb uses
            it under the BSD License.                https://facebook.github.io/zstd/
  liburing  MIT License. liburing is dual licensed LGPL-2.1 and MIT; tsdb
            uses it under MIT.                       https://github.com/axboe/liburing
  libgcc    linked statically (-static-libgcc) under the GCC Runtime Library
            Exception, which allows this without carrying the GPL text.

The C library (glibc) is not part of the tarball: the binaries use the one of
the machine they run on.

The libraries in lib/ (libtsdb.a, libtsdbclient.a) contain tsdb code only. A
program that links them also links its own libzstd.

docs/licenses.md in the source repository lists every dependency of tsdb, its
clients and the Pulsar connector.


